Geographic data sources and notices

The bundled GeoJSON files are simplified visualization copies. They are not
survey documents or legal boundary descriptions. The bloomr MIT license covers
package code and documentation; it does not claim ownership of source geography.

New Jersey state, county, and municipal boundaries:
  Source: New Jersey Office of Information Technology, Office of GIS (NJOGIS).
  Government Boundaries service:
  https://maps.nj.gov/arcgis/rest/services/Framework/Government_Boundaries/MapServer
  Municipal boundaries metadata:
  https://www.arcgis.com/sharing/rest/content/items/1c6b26a9a14e4132895194e80d6b30f8/info/metadata/metadata.xml?format=default&output=html
  NJOGIS requests acknowledgement in maps, data, and other products derived
  from its data. Boundaries are not authoritative for legal or survey use.

Texas state, county, and county subdivision boundaries:
  Source: U.S. Census Bureau, 2025 TIGER/Line county subdivision shapefiles.
  https://www.census.gov/geographies/mapping-files/time-series/geo/tiger-line-file.2025.html
  The bundled state and counties were derived by dissolving subdivisions.
  TIGER/Line® is a registered trademark of the U.S. Census Bureau. Its use here
  identifies the source data; it does not imply Census Bureau endorsement.
  Census boundaries are for statistical purposes and are not legal land
  descriptions. The Census Bureau requests citation when its data are reused.
